      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# ⚗ T2I · Krea 2\n**Write an idea → Queue.** Load → LoRA Stack+ → Prompt → KSampler Flex → Save.\n\n1. **Load**: Krea 2 Turbo + Qwen3-VL-4B text encoder + Qwen-Image VAE (any Krea 2 fine-tune works too).\n2. **LoRA Stack+**: ➕ *Add LoRA*, click the name to pick it with previews, ▲ ▼ to try the next one. The number is the real strength; ● = on/off; green `T` = trigger words added to the prompt.\n3. **Prompt**: an *idea* in any language, Krea 2's own encoder writes the prompt (`mode → as written` keeps your text). At the bottom: **shot / camera angle / view / light / atmosphere / background** presets, with thumbnails (📷). `⚙ compact view` shows every option.\n4. **KSampler Flex**: leave it as is. `profile (auto)` uses your calibration if you ran one (`KREA2_TARATURA`), otherwise an analytic schedule (the report says which).\n5. **Save**: 📁 to pick drive and folder.\n\nTips: strong LoRAs and wet-looking skin → `variety` 0.2-0.3 · faster → `megapixels` 2.5 · more people than asked in wide frames → the Prompt adds a guard by itself.\n\n**Different, not better.** On the same seed the Alchemica recipe gives *another* picture than ComfyUI's KSampler: other composition, more fine detail, sometimes a more \"illustrated\" look. If you prefer the plain result, set `sampler_name` **euler** and `scheduler` **simple** in KSampler Flex and turn `two_stage` off: same node, standard sampling. Compare both on your own prompts (`KREA2_CONFRONTO_ONESTO`).\n\n⚗ Idea & direction: **AlchemicaMente** · code: **Claude (Anthropic)** · [ComfyUI-AlchemicaSampler](https://github.com/Nessuno76/ComfyUI-AlchemicaSampler) · GPL-3.0"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "### ⚗ Quick guide\n1. **Load** – Krea 2 Turbo + Qwen3-VL text encoder + Qwen-Image VAE.\n2. **LoRA** – up to 6, `(none)` = off.\n3. **Prompt** – write an *idea* (any language): Krea 2's own encoder writes the prompt. `mode → as written` to keep your text. Format: `aspect` + `megapixels`. NAG on = the negative works at cfg 1.\n4. **Sampler** – leave it as is: `profile (auto)` + `alchemica_calibrated` + calibration **v2** use the step spacing measured on your checkpoint. Two stages, resolution-corrected hand-off and **DeGrid** (Krea 2 VAE grid fix) are on.\n5. **Save** – pick drive and folder with 📁 *Browse folders…*; the file takes the workflow's name.\n\n**Tips** · more quality: `steps` 10-12 · more variety between seeds: `variety` 0.6 · strong LoRAs with \"wet\" skin: `variety` 0.15-0.2 · no profile yet? run *⚗ Alchemica Calibration* once on your checkpoint."
      },
      "color": "#2a2a2a",
      "bgcolor": "#1c1c1c"
    },
